{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558165-beast-how-exactly-do-lairs-work","id":558165,"title":"Beast: How exactly do Lairs work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-17T06:43:05-07:00","id":558165,"title":"Beast: How exactly do Lairs work?","content":"I'm confused how a Beast enters his Lair and merges with his Horror. For instance if I wanted to do so in order to heal.<br /> <br /> quote:<br /> -Healing in the Lair<br /> Beasts can enter their Lairs, merge with the Souls (Horror), and repair their bodies very quickly. This leaves them hungry, however. A Beast in her Lair can spend one point of Satiety to heal all bashing damage; three points of lethal damage, or one point of aggravated damage. If the Beast currently has multiple types of damage, the player chooses which to heal, but can\u2019t heal different types with one expenditure. For example, a Beast with three points of aggravated damage and two lethal damage would have to spend four dots of Satiety (one for each aggravated and one for the lethal) to heal it all.-<br /> <br /> <br /> How does one enter their Lairs and merge with their Souls (Horrors)?<br /> <br /> quote:<br /> -Accessing the Lair<br /> An empty Lair is just a stage devoid of action, with the Beast\u2019s Soul (Horror) wandering from Chamber to Chamber. The Soul (Horror) is capable of acting independently, but Beasts can see through the Soul\u2019s (Horror's) eyes and direct its actions at any time, or vanish from the physical world entirely and fully inhabit their Primordial self.-<br /> <br /> Is this just the heading for the next group of abilities, like the Primordial Pathway? Because nowhere in the rest of the chapter does it discuss merging with the Soul (Horror) or 'Fully inhabit their Primordial self'. Except in the description of opening a Primordial Pathway.<br /> <br /> quote:<br /> -Pathways aren\u2019t portals or magical doors. When opened, the Pathway causes the Chamber and the external location to \u201coverlap.\u201d This causes Beasts to merge with their Souls (Horror), as described on p. XX. Anyone in the external location attempting to leave while the Pathway is active instead finds themselves transitioning to another Chamber through one of the Lair\u2019s Burrows. Anyone still in the Chamber when the Pathway closes ends up in the external location. Collapsing a Chamber immediately closes any Primordial Pathways open to it.<br /> <br /> Now, since I don't know what page XX. is referencing, I'm not sure where to look.<br /> <br /> If a Beast must open a Primordial Pathway every time the want to enter their lair, they must spend a Willpower Point every time as well?<br /> <br /> How long can they stay in their Lair, merged with their Soul (Horror)?<br /> <br /> Do they need to open a Primordial Pathway and spend another Willpower Piint and roll to leave and go back to the material world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2545-ninjar","name":"Ninjar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2545_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T06:47:36-07:00","id":558195,"title":"","content":"Accessing Lair text mentions that they can do it easily from the location of their chamber. Any other location requires spending a point of WP. <br /> <br /> So, at least how I run it, if you go to the location for your Lair chamber, then there's no cost to try and get your Lair to overlap. if you wanna do it from another place, then you get to roll and you get penalties/bonuses depending on how similar it is to the actual chamber/circumstance of the chamber. <br /> Beast can stay in their Lairs indefinitely. However, most Beasts will have to go out of their Lair from time to time (to feed).<br /> When leaving, they do it for free, if they leave back to their chamber, or they spend willpower if they want to go somewhere else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T07:48:09-07:00","id":558231,"title":"","content":"How do Lairs work? Awesomely well! *cough* Okay, truthfully I don't know yet, but I want to try it out.<br /> <br /> How to enter the Lair:<br /> <br /> There are four methods. The first one is Soul Communion - just spend a reflexive action to look through your Soul's eyes, or a full action to control your Soul. You're not physically there, so you can't heal, but it may be relevant for other uses, such as potentially spying on someone's onerios from within your Lair.<br /> <br /> The second is to use a Skeleton Key. You'll somehow need to know the location of a Bolthole, Locus, Trod, or Avernian gate (likely by being told by a demon, wolf, changeling, or sin-eater) since you can't sense them on your own, but you can open them. <br /> <br /> Third is the Under the Bed method. Its a bit more complicated than the others - first, you have to indulge your Hunger in front of someone, then spend 1 willpower to make a connection. Whenever the target goes to sleep, you can walk up to the person, spend 1 Satiety, and jump in. There's a few more requirements, such as the target has to suspect you're responcable for causing the initial problems, may need the Family Ties Condition, causes nightmares and hostility in target, and may create a Hero through use. Generally, I think this is best if you have a favorite target to pick on long term, and the entering Lair part is incidental to messing with someone's head.<br /> <br /> Lastly, there's what I like to think of as the default method. Go to somewhere you made a Lair Chamber, or somewhere that resonates with your Lair (ie has one of the Lair Traits). Spend a point of willpower and roll; I think you need an additional willpower point if its just similar instead the exact place, making the total 2*. This way drags everyone into the Lair as the physical and Primordial Dream worlds merge. I consider the same qualifications you need for Imposing Traits (Beast p122) to apply to opening a Primordial Pathway. From the way the section is worded, I think that if the Beast is still in the initial Chamber when she closes the Pathway, she's ejected with everyone else back into reality. However, if anyone moves into another Chamber and then closes the connection, anyone in that second chamber stays in the Primordial Dream Lair.<br /> <br /> Now, for the next question. How long can you stay? Well, I assume that you're going to still need to fulfill your physical body's needs - its a merger, not a supplement. So, you'll need food, water, etc. You still need to feed your Satiety, though if you can reach from your lair to haunt dreams and feed that way, that's not a pressing issue. As long as you account for those things, I'd say you can stay in the Lair indefinitely. <br /> <br /> If you're using the Primordial Pathway method, you need to spend a willpower point every time you use the Path, and, yes, you need to open a new path (complete with willpower point*) to leave the Dream as well. <br /> <br /> <br /> * I could be mistaken about needing a willpower point by default, and an extra for someplace that's just resonant. If you only need 1 willpower to open up in a resonant area, and none for the original chamber, then you could open and close pathways to and from the Dream at will, basically. So, if you use the Pathway to get to the dream from Anywhere (TM), you can chill in the Lair, then go back to your Chamber Creation points at will. <br /> <br /> This is a reason why I think that a smart Beast will establish their Safe Place merit at the location of these exit points. Impose all the Traits, all the time! It gets scary with a brood doing this and sharing that one Safe Place trait in common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T08:10:16-07:00","id":558278,"title":"","content":"quote<br /> -Now, for the next question. How long can you stay? Well, I assume that you're going to still need to fulfill your physical body's needs - its a merger, not a supplement. So, you'll need food, water, etc. You still need to feed your Satiety, though if you can reach from your lair to haunt dreams and feed that way, that's not a pressing issue. As long as you account for those things, I'd say you can stay in the Lair indefinitely.-<br /> <br /> This is the part that is very confusing to me and my group. According to the example given under the Primordial Pathways ability, it says this:<br /> <br /> quote<br /> -<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Killing one of the other hunters, the Anakim closes the Pathway \u2014 the school returns to normal, the Beast appears to transform back into his mortal body as he separates from his Soul again, and the remaining hunter who stayed returns as well. The hunter who left the Chamber, however, remains behind in the Lair, easy pickings for the Anakim\u2019s Soul.-<br /> <br /> Since the Pathway only stays open for a number of turns equal to the Beast's Resolve, he seems to be limited to a few seconds. Does that mean, he needs to go into another Chamber before the Pathway closes in order to stay in the Lair? Kind of like how the third Hunter was stuck after moving to the other Chamber?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2545-ninjar","name":"Ninjar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2545_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T08:24:39-07:00","id":558286,"title":"","content":"My assumption is that when a primordial pathway closes the beast can just choose which side of it they end up on. <br /> <br /> As for food and water, well most lairs will probably have chambers with one or the other in them. Lakes, trees, stuff like that. If that's not enough you could probably drag real food in if you wanted to. Keep a fridge in your Heart powered by a waterwheel or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T08:30:59-07:00","id":558294,"title":"","content":"When you open the Passway, you're not really in the Lair at point, you're kind of in an unstable halfway border realm. Its like crossing the Gauntlet - you need to move a bit deeper before you actually enter the Otherworld proper.<br /> <br /> When you open a Passway, its like opening a door and getting a blast of hot air as well as sound from the party inside. If the Passway closes before you do move deeper, its the equivalent of the door slamming in your face while you stood outside. You actually have to move past the doorway to get inside.<br /> <br /> <br /> We might not be talking about a literal portal, but it does act a lot like one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T08:44:16-07:00","id":558303,"title":"","content":"MCN- This is the impression I am getting as well.<br /> <br /> Now, what if you only have a Heart Chamber, because a starting character can sacrifice their additional Chamber for 2XP.<br /> <br /> Can a Character with only their Heart Chamber actually stay inside their lair? They can't move to another Chamber once they open a Primordial Pathway after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2545-ninjar","name":"Ninjar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2545_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T08:46:00-07:00","id":558305,"title":"","content":"They can if they're part of a brood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T09:00:30-07:00","id":558317,"title":"","content":"What Elfive said. Plus, I personally don't have a problem with someone descriptively &quot;moving deeper into the Chamber&quot; without actually leaving it. There's all sorts of burrows and connections even in the Heart that we can approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T09:15:34-07:00","id":558324,"title":"","content":"I think the best rule of thumb is to say &quot;you can't just vanish&quot;. If you're entering on your own or holding the door, who cares about how deep you go? You open the pathway, you're in. No problem. If you have intruders you're trying to shake, <i>then</i> you need to get out of sight somehow. Either go into another chamber or just go through a door and close it, so when the pathway closes and they follow you through, you're just gone with no explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T09:31:30-07:00","id":558345,"title":"","content":"So, what I am getting from you all, is that there does need to be a little clarification regarding these aspects of the Lair.<br /> <br /> When using 'Holding the Door' and 'Be My Guest' we have to assume the Beast needs to escort his guests into another Chamber for them to remain in the Lair for more than a few seconds. If they stay in the original location used with Primordial Pathway, then they will fade back into the world after a few seconds.<br /> <br /> Another thought. Perhaps the 'place' that opens during Primordial Pathway isn't actually a Chamber, but a generic aspect of the Lair in general. It has Lair Traits and allows the Beast to merge with their Horror, but is otherwise not a Chamber or Burrow but a temporary bridge between the material world and the Lair. When a Beast (or guests using Holding the Door and Be My Guest) then 'step through' they actually enter a Chamber and are inside the Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2545-ninjar","name":"Ninjar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2545_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T20:31:01-07:00","id":559018,"title":"","content":"I would guess the clock on food, water, etc. is paused while in a Lair. It isn't like there would actually be any air in a dream world. I actually wouldn't expect a Beast to need to sleep nor would they age while inside. I'm working under the assumption that the Beast becomes a dream. Info on the Primordial Dream is sketchy so far. Very difficult to say how all that works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T10:38:25-07:00","id":559536,"title":"","content":"It's not only the metaphysical aspects that are confusing, but mechanical aspects of the game.<br /> <br /> That's what I can't figure out.<br /> <br /> Step by step, can somebody break down how a Beast enters his own Lair? Let's say, in order to Heal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2545-ninjar","name":"Ninjar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2545_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T10:54:44-07:00","id":559563,"title":"","content":"Like MCN did? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T11:26:37-07:00","id":559599,"title":"","content":"This is a repost of something I put in Ninjar's game (I'm one of the players of the playtest he's running). It might show more about some of the things we're pondering.<br /> <br /> &quot;I think you can enter your Heart from anywhere, but you have a much easier time if it corresponds with your lair's resonance. Other chambers though, are set to specific locations.<br /> <br /> When you open a pathway, the Lair overlaps with wherever you are, so we'd be both in your Lair and the other location at the same time.<br /> <br /> Here's a thought. You can open Chambers to other worlds then the Material one, so the Lair would also become a transit hub. You could travel there, open a new Chamber and then tie it to the Shadow or the Astral plane and travel there.<br /> <br /> And.. oh. Maybe I got this wrong. It looks like you only need to spend WP if you're entering your Lair from a point you haven't set a previous connection to, or maybe the WP is for creating an entirely new connection when you set up a new Chamber?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T13:44:35-07:00","id":559750,"title":"","content":"You can enter any chamber including the heart from any location that resonates with the chamber, but this costs a willpower point. If you use the location you created the chamber at then you don't spend the willpower. The heart is not tied to any location.<br /> <br /> The chamber overlaps with the location you are opening a pathway to or from.<br /> <br /> You can open a pathway to and from other worlds the same as the material one. You can also create chambers from locations in other worlds the same as the material one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:18:22-07:00","id":559844,"title":"","content":"That sounds all good, but <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">seems to be inconsistent with the example for Primordial Pathways.</span></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_med\" align=\"center\" style=\"height: 14px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_med_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_med_td\"><b>Example::</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_quote text_table_med_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_med_td text_table_quote_td\" style=\"background-color: #E8E8E8\">A Tyrant Anakim whose Soul preys on childhood fears has incorporated an abandoned high school as a Chamber in his Lair. On the run from a group of mortal monsterhunters (though not, thankfully, Heroes) he leads his pursuers into the school and opens the Primordial Pathway. For a few seconds, the interior of the school becomes both in the material world and the Chamber in his Lair, and the Anakim immediately merges with his Soul. Faced by the hulking monster where their target once stood, the hunters panic. Two gird themselves and fight, and the third attempts to flee the school, but while the Pathway is still open she instead transitions through a Burrow into another Chamber. Killing one of the other hunters, the Anakim closes the Pathway \u2014 the school returns to normal, the Beast appears to transform back into his mortal body as he separates from his Soul again, and the remaining hunter who stayed returns as well. The hunter who left the Chamber, however, remains behind in the Lair, easy pickings for the Anakim\u2019s Soul.</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Lets pull this thing apart and see what is happening.</span></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_med\" align=\"center\" style=\"height: 14px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_med_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_med_td\"><b>Example::</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_quote text_table_med_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_med_td text_table_quote_td\" style=\"background-color: #E8E8E8\">A Tyrant Anakim whose Soul preys on childhood fears has incorporated an abandoned high school as a Chamber in his Lair. On the run from a group of mortal monsterhunters (though not, thankfully, Heroes) he leads his pursuers into the school and opens the Primordial Pathway.</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">The Beast is opening a Primordial Pathway between the high school and his Chamber. Does he roll, spend Willpower? You say yes, so lets move on.</span></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_med\" align=\"center\" style=\"height: 14px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_med_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_med_td\"><b>Example::</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_quote text_table_med_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_med_td text_table_quote_td\" style=\"background-color: #E8E8E8\">For a few seconds, the interior of the school becomes both in the material world and the Chamber in his Lair, and the Anakim immediately merges with his Soul. Faced by the hulking monster where their target once stood, the hunters panic.</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">So the Pathway opens for a number of turns equal to the Beast's Resolve (a few seconds)</span></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_med\" align=\"center\" style=\"height: 14px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_med_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_med_td\"><b>Example::</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_quote text_table_med_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_med_td text_table_quote_td\" style=\"background-color: #E8E8E8\">Two gird themselves and fight, and the third attempts to flee the school, but while the Pathway is still open she instead transitions through a Burrow into another Chamber.</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">This is an effect of the ability, that those that try to leave are transported into another Chamber of the Lair.</span></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_med\" align=\"center\" style=\"height: 14px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_med_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_med_td\"><b>Example::</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_quote text_table_med_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_med_td text_table_quote_td\" style=\"background-color: #E8E8E8\">Killing one of the other hunters, the Anakim closes the Pathway \u2014 the school returns to normal, the Beast appears to transform back into his mortal body as he separates from his Soul again, and the remaining hunter who stayed returns as well. The hunter who left the Chamber, however, remains behind in the Lair, easy pickings for the Anakim\u2019s Soul.</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">So, as soon as the Primordial Pathway closes, the Beast appears to transform back into his mortal body. He doesn't stay there with his Horror or with anyone left inside. Also, the one hunter who didn't flee returns back to the normal High School.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">The only person to actually stay inside the Lair is the one who fled to a different chamber and he is left to deal with the Beast's Horror, not the Beast himself.<br /> <br /> Could the Beast stay inside his Lair if he chose to? Or does he always automatically leave.</span></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_med\" align=\"center\" style=\"height: 14px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_med_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_med_td\"><b>My Player Commented:</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_quote text_table_med_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_med_td text_table_quote_td\" style=\"background-color: #E8E8E8\">They have to. They can bring human beings to thier lairs-they have powers relating to that. Heck, they get a +1 feeding modifier when they do...</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">It would appear that they don't and they might only get that bonus for the few seconds that the Primordial Pathway is open. If they successfully feed while its open, they get the +1 to their Satiety Roll.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">That's what I'm reading from this.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2545-ninjar","name":"Ninjar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2545_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:12:51-07:00","id":559993,"title":"","content":"What was inconsistent? As I read it, the pathway is going from the location the chamber was made from to that chamber, the beast doesn't need to roll or spend willpower. It automatically happens for free. That is the special case. The rest seems correct. It does not specify that a Beast can stay, but it makes sense for it to work that way. All a Beast would have to do is take a burrow to a different chamber and wait for the pathway to close to stay. I don't see how it is any real advantage to be able to choose to stay without switching to another chamber. I think the Beast, Brood, and invited guests would all get to choose to stay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:42:39-07:00","id":560036,"title":"","content":"See, those are a lot of the 'assumptions' I had when reading it, but nowhere in the text does it specifically say these key things. The best that I can see are these portions of the text under Primordial Pathways.<br /> <br /> 1. A Beast does not need to roll or spend Willpower to activate Primordial Pathways in the location a Chamber was created. Does easy equal no roll, no Willpower?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Opening a Pathway to the exact location the Beast created a Chamber from is <b>easiest</b>, but desperate Beasts and cunning would-be intruders can use locations that are similar by spending a point of Willpower during the attempt and incurring an additional dice penalty based on how well the location matches (see p. XX.) </div> </div> </div>2. That the Beast can stay 'inside' his Lair after the Primordial Pathways duration expires. Must the Beast move to another Chamber?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Success: The Pathway successfully opens and lasts for the opening character\u2019s Resolve in turns. </div> </div> </div>3. That the Beast or his Invited Guests can't stay in the originating Chamber or in the Lair at all, unless they move to a different Chamber.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyone in the external location attempting to leave while the Pathway is active instead finds themselves transitioning to another Chamber through one of the Lair\u2019s Burrows. Anyone still in the Chamber when the Pathway closes ends up in the external location. </div> </div> </div>I think that since Lairs play such a crucial role in the game, the primary ability to access it should be much clearer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2545-ninjar","name":"Ninjar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2545_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T19:17:11-07:00","id":560204,"title":"","content":"Since it only mentions spending willpower when its not the exact location and that comes after mentioning exact locations, it should be inferred that it doesn't require willpower. If it did then they would need to clarify it. Similarly about not having to roll, there is no mention of a bonus for an exact location. If you were meant to roll then a bonus should be indicated as it does specifically state exact locations are easier. Your feeling of how it should work is right, unless it gets changed.<br /> <br /> I don't see why the Beast would have to move to another Chamber. If the Beast does move then they would be stuck in their Lair when the pathway closes. Why force the Beast to move just for that purpose? The difference would be trivial.<br /> <br /> Invited Guests and Brood mates get to move around as easily as the Beast wants. They can use Burrows freely and can be immune to Lair traits while in the Lair. It only makes sense to me for the guests to stay if the Beast wants them to stay and the guest wants to stay.<br /> <br /> Every book ends up with some vague and confusing parts. I would save this as a note and bring it up after the kickstarter is over. They have an editing phase and they usually start a FAQ then too.<br /> <br /> You have valid questions but I think you will have to wait a while to get an official answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T19:30:23-07:00","id":560213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558165-beast-how-exactly-do-lairs-work?p=560204#post560204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since it only mentions spending willpower when its not the exact location and that comes after mentioning exact locations, it should be inferred that it doesn't require willpower. If it did then they would need to clarify it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Note that the roll section lists 1 willpower for cost. So, no matter when you roll, the implication is that it costs 1 willpower there. So... it is a bit unclear. Hopefully the final draft will be a bit cleaner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T19:49:46-07:00","id":560245,"title":"","content":"I've asked a few times in the KS comments and haven't gotten any response. Guess I'll wait and see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2545-ninjar","name":"Ninjar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2545_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:51:03-07:00","id":560298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558165-beast-how-exactly-do-lairs-work?p=560213#post560213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Note that the roll section lists 1 willpower for cost. So, no matter when you roll, the implication is that it costs 1 willpower there. So... it is a bit unclear. Hopefully the final draft will be a bit cleaner.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you don't roll if it is the exact location so all of the stuff about rolling would be irrelevant. If you have to roll then there is nothing to actually make it easier if it is the exact location. I don't dispute that something is missing for clarity. You have to make something up no matter how you look at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T08:26:20-07:00","id":560866,"title":"","content":"&quot;A Tyrant Anakim whose Soul preys on childhood fears has incorporated an abandoned high school as a Chamber in his Lair&quot;<br /> &quot;Two gird themselves and fight, and the third attempts to flee the school, but while the Pathway is still open she instead transitions through a Burrow into another Chamber.&quot;<br /> &quot;Success: The Pathway successfully opens and lasts for the opening character\u2019s Resolve in turns. &quot;<br /> <br /> We know that a turn is equal to 3 seconds.<br /> A beast may have 1 resolve.<br /> My personal experience with high school was that i surely could not exit it in only 3 seconds unless i was already at the entrance/exit.<br /> So, the mortal hunter fleeing the Anakim in the above example was either near an entrance/exit, had supernatural powers of movement, or simply moved deeper into the chamber (i.e didnt stay in the same classroom, or hallway but was still inside the high school). To me it makes sense that when you merge a chamber and a location, the only way to NOT move further into the lair is by staying put in the room (i.e. classroom, outcropping, clearing of forest) you happen to be in, until the effect ends. And practically if you were an invited guest, hunting the beast or simply trying to access your own lair, taking a few steps &quot;deeper&quot; into the chamber would be sufficient to cross the &quot;portal doorway&quot;. While if you did not wish to stay, and had the sense not to run away screaming in horror, you could simply stay in the relative &quot;room&quot; you are in until the effects end and then not be stuck in the primordial dream lair of a scary monster.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2741-hemophage","name":"Hemophage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T13:54:00-07:00","id":562184,"title":"","content":"I am confused about how your character appears when they are in the lair, parts of it refer to the character transforming and other parts don't which is confusing. So here is my question &quot;I&quot; the character enter my lair, do I A: transform into my beast form or B: remain in my mortal host form. Now i am aware there are merging rules but from what i took away from it is that is final character action for the most part making your character an NPC","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T13:57:08-07:00","id":562188,"title":"","content":"No, you control your Horror when you merge with it. You can control it when you're separate as well, if you concentrate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T15:29:38-07:00","id":562275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558165-beast-how-exactly-do-lairs-work?p=562184#post562184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am confused about how your character appears when they are in the lair, parts of it refer to the character transforming and other parts don't which is confusing. So here is my question &quot;I&quot; the character enter my lair, do I A: transform into my beast form or B: remain in my mortal host form. Now i am aware there are merging rules but from what i took away from it is that is final character action for the most part making your character an NPC</div> </div> </div> </div>Complete and permanent merger is an end of character thing, but anytime you enter your lair you merge with the Horror. It just gets called a transformation because it looks like that from the perspective of outsiders.<br /> Oh unless your Horror is in a food coma then if you go into your lair the two of you are separate entities until you wake it up and your lair is just as deadly to you as everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T14:55:06-07:00","id":569666,"title":"","content":"The revision clarifies that you always roll and spend willpower for primordial pathways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T15:22:50-07:00","id":569695,"title":"","content":"Wait have they released another chapter? I can't find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T15:25:50-07:00","id":569696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558165-beast-how-exactly-do-lairs-work?p=569666#post569666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The revision clarifies that you always roll and spend willpower for primordial pathways.</div> </div> </div> </div>No clarification has occurred regarding Willpower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558165-beast-how-exactly-do-lairs-work?p=569695#post569695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait have they released another chapter? I can't find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the same Drive folder as the first three, as is Chapter Four.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-26-2015, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T16:16:54-07:00","id":569747,"title":"","content":"Awesome. Let's have a look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T16:26:07-07:00","id":569775,"title":"","content":"They added the linked location to the chart. That means you always roll and since the roll lists willpower as a cost without exception, I think it is pretty clear. I suppose the text could be more clear, but I can follow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T16:47:06-07:00","id":569785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558165-beast-how-exactly-do-lairs-work?p=569775#post569775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They added the linked location to the chart. That means you always roll and since the roll lists willpower as a cost without exception, I think it is pretty clear. I suppose the text could be more clear, but I can follow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally nothing about the ambiguous text preceding the roll description is different, which was the entire basis of people being confused about whether the roll description listing a Willpower cost superseded the paragraph's implication that using a substitute location was what added a Willpower cost to the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T17:05:00-07:00","id":569791,"title":"","content":"The intent is clear even if there is a strangely worded sentence creating some confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T18:02:00-07:00","id":569812,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, the intent is crystal clear. It's <i>definitely</i> the opposite of what you think it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T18:19:04-07:00","id":569815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558165-beast-how-exactly-do-lairs-work?p=569812#post569812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yeah, the intent is crystal clear. It's <i>definitely</i> the opposite of what you think it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of intent, reading the revisions has prompted the realization that the Wits + Resolve roll for imposing Lair Traits modified by Chamber resonance is kind of unclear.<br /> <br /> Do you only roll if you're imposing Traits without an existing Tilt? Is the Willpower point for a substitute location on top of or in place of the Satiety expenditure you'd make if you were just using the Chamber's basis directly?<br /> <br /> Also, how does the new qualifier for Chamberhood influence the distinction between spiritual and narrative similarity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T18:22:01-07:00","id":569816,"title":"","content":"It is opposite of what I thought it was. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> And from what the text suggests, but mechanics trump fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T18:38:18-07:00","id":569835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558165-beast-how-exactly-do-lairs-work?p=569815#post569815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of intent, reading the revisions has prompted the realization that the Wits + Resolve roll for imposing Lair Traits modified by Chamber resonance is kind of unclear.<br /> <br /> Do you only roll if you're imposing Traits without an existing Tilt? Is the Willpower point for a substitute location on top of or in place of the Satiety expenditure you'd make if you were just using the Chamber's basis directly?<br /> <br /> Also, how does the new qualifier for Chamberhood influence the distinction between spiritual and narrative similarity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unclear. I think you always roll, the willpower is in addition to the Satiety, and I don't understand the last question. What is the context?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T20:09:12-07:00","id":569859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558165-beast-how-exactly-do-lairs-work?p=569835#post569835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand the last question. What is the context?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the first draft, there were two ways you could incorporate a location with one of your Lair Traits into your Lair as a Chamber: another character must have lost Integrity-or-a-suitable-analogue or you must have gotten an exceptional success on a Nightmare roll.<br /> <br /> The current draft has adjusted this such that the former must have happened while you were present, and a third category now exists to complement the existence of freestanding Chambers, which means that if you got a given Chamber by playing Jungian scavenger a question now exists of how one recreates the confrontation with the Primordial Dream that distinguishes the \u20134 penalty of narrative similarity from the \u20132 penalty of spiritual similarity.<br /> <br /> This question exists because incorporating that Chamber required you to track down information about a specific supernatural being which may have generated the Chamber through means beyond the Begotten's ability to replicate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T21:44:27-07:00","id":569932,"title":"","content":"I think I follow. I believe that question existed before too. I'm guessing when the Beast isn't causing the breaking point originally then they can go for narrative, and not spiritual, similarity. I think it would have to work that way whenever the Beast didn't use Nightmare to make the location suitable for a Chamber. There might be a niche case where spiritual similarity is possible, but generally it seems out of bounds. If the Beast is taking the role of another person, that seems like it would be narrative rather than spiritual. Great question. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T01:07:22-07:00","id":570028,"title":"","content":"Some chambers are just easier to get in than others, I guess. <br /> <br /> Also the text in question regarding that isn't fluff. It's just mechanics written out. You can't talk about spending willpower in the fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T01:30:05-07:00","id":570032,"title":"","content":"You can and they did. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I'll take charts over awkwardly, and apparently inappropriately, worded text. I will grant you that if they removed the bit about willpower from the text then there would be no confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T03:03:40-07:00","id":570089,"title":"","content":"It's in there twice, you know. The bit about imposing lair traits uses the exact same wording.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As with opening a Primordial Pathway, Beasts may attempt to use a Chamber in locations that are similar, if not exactly the same, by spending a Willpower point. </div> </div> </div>This phrasing is not at all ambiguous. It says a willpower point. not an <i>additional </i>willpower point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T05:11:31-07:00","id":570165,"title":"","content":"Who said anything about additional willpower? It was always just one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T05:25:53-07:00","id":570168,"title":"","content":"Then they wouldn't have mentioned the willpower at all. They're clearly making a <i>distinction</i> here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T05:38:16-07:00","id":570171,"title":"","content":"It's just wonky wording. With lair traits, you spend Satiety then sometimes willpower. Pathways is just willpower. In pathways they should nix mentioning willpower in the text and deal with it at the roll info. If it ever costs more than one willpower that would be the place to state it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T05:42:31-07:00","id":570182,"title":"","content":"The wording is not wonky you're just reading it wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T06:05:07-07:00","id":570186,"title":"","content":"Possible. It would seem I'm reading what you write wrong unless you are saying it sometimes costs more than one willpower for pathways and only ever costs one willpower. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T06:18:07-07:00","id":570190,"title":"","content":"I'm saying it sometimes doesn't cost any. The Willpower is definitely, unambiguously, an extra cost. There would be no reason whatsoever to phrase it the way they phrase it if it wasn't. The <i>only</i> way for accessing the lair from a place you made a chamber to cost one willpower is if accessing it from anywhere else costs two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T06:43:52-07:00","id":570225,"title":"","content":"That is what I have always said the text suggests. However, since they added the exact location to the chart for rolling when you do pathways and the cost was not updated to say &quot;except when going to/from the exact location...&quot; then the text seems to be in error.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T06:59:36-07:00","id":570240,"title":"","content":"Most of the places on the chart are going to cost willpower. If they had an exception for one specific circumstance they's just spell it out in the text above like how they said one end has to be in the lair, and whoops, there it is. IT'S NOT FLUFF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T07:15:10-07:00","id":570245,"title":"","content":"I guess they didn't clear it up then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}